description: Shikshakalay shared project rules (always on)
alwaysApply: true
---
Before writing any code, read and follow `AGENTS.md` in the repo root. It is the single source of truth:
the product, the hackathon rules, the stack, folder owners (P1/P2/P3), the engine rules, the API list and the
"do not" list. The shared types in `src/lib/contracts.ts` win over everything else.

- Stay inside the folders your person owns (AGENTS.md section 6). Ask before touching anyone else's files.
- Never change `src/lib/contracts.ts` without a PR all three people approve.
- The engine decides every child's answer in TypeScript; Claude only writes the words.
- No keys, phone numbers, real names or real recordings in git or logs. Mock mode (`USE_MOCKS=1`) must keep working.
- Before saying a task is done: `npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test`.
- Next.js here is v16 and newer than your training data: check `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` when unsure.
